* Simple GPL "Hello World" with background color change
       GROM >6000
       AORG >0000

* Cartridge header
       DATA >AA01         * Valid cartridge
       DATA 0,0,0
       DATA MENU          * Pointer to menu
       DATA 0,0,0,0

MENU   DATA 0             * Next menu item (none)
       DATA START         * Entry point
       STRI 'HELLO GPL'   * Menu title (length byte auto-added by STRI)
       BSS 0              

* Main program
START  ALL >20            * Clear screen with spaces (char >20)
       BACK >1F           * Background dark blue (low nibble), black text (high nibble)

* Load standard character patterns (ASCII 32-95 and 96-126)
       DST >0900,@>834A   * Pattern table address for chars 32-95
       CALL >0018
       DST >0B00,@>834A   * Pattern table address for chars 96-126
       CALL >004A

* Display "Hello World" centered using FMT mode
       FMT
       ROW 12             * Row 12 (0-based, roughly center)
       COL 11             * Column for centering ~11 chars
       HTEX 'Hello World' ; Horizontal text
       FEND

* Wait for keypress then exit
LOOP   SCAN               * Scan keyboard
       BR LOOP            * Loop if no new key
       EXIT               * Quit back to title screen

       END